sitory: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-50\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sketches\" kind=\"sketches\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff use one shared platform to receive and track stock, process customer orders, plan and record deliveries, view temperature histories, make quality decisions, and manage recalls; changes to stock availability, orders, delivery progress, temperature status, and recall status are reflected in the relevant workflows.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can see when stock or an order cannot proceed because it is quarantined, on hold, rejected, recalled, expired, or otherwise unavailable, rather than being able to treat it as usable.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The platform retains records of operational and quality decisions so an inspector can review who acted and when.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Warehouse operators can record receipts, storage movements, picks, and packing for warehouses to which they are assigned.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Dispatchers can allocate or override stock choices with a reason, plan routes, assign drivers and vehicles, and follow delivery progress for their permitted warehouses.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Quality officers can review temperature evidence and propose stock dispositions; quality managers can approve quality decisions and start or close recalls.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System administrators can manage staff accounts, warehouses, vehicles, shipper types, products, and system configuration; auditors can view records and audit history but cannot create, change, or delete records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each portal page and its controls remain usable at phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user without the relevant role or warehouse assignment cannot perform or view the restricted operation or record.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-3\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An authenticated hospital, pharmacy, or clinic user can place orders for their organisation, choose one of its saved delivery addresses and a permitted delivery date, select whether available quantities may be delivered or the order must be complete, and view order status and allocated and outstanding quantities.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer users can change or cancel an order until packing begins; after packing begins, the customer is refused the change or cancellation and can see that the order is no longer customer-editable.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer administrators can invite and remove users belonging to their own organisation; users from another organisation and customer users without administrator authority cannot administer those accounts.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer user sees only their organisation's orders, deliveries, and documents, including relevant delivery and quality case information; requests for another organisation's records are denied.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Submitting the same order twice by mistake results in one order rather than duplicate orders.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A deactivated product, invalid quantity, missing order line, unconfigured address, or too-early delivery date is rejected with an explanation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-4\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A signed-in driver can open and work the current day's route in the responsive web experience when the network is unavailable, including viewing the route and recording work that can be synchronized later.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When connectivity returns, recorded offline work is synchronized and the driver can see whether it was accepted or needs attention; the system does not silently discard unsynchronized entries.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A driver whose account has been disabled or removed is denied access when online; actions queued while offline are not treated as proof that access remains authorized once the system can verify the account.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When offline, the driver sees that data or actions cannot yet be verified or synchronized, rather than being shown a false confirmation that the server has accepted them.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The requested driver application is delivered as the same responsive web app, usable in a phone browser with offline route access, not as a native app.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-5\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system accepts temperature readings sent through the logger supplier's gateway for known logger and cold-room sensor devices and adds valid readings to the relevant device history.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A reading received more than once is represented once in the history; late and out-of-order readings are placed according to the time they were taken and trigger recalculation of affected temperature assessments.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Readings with a future timestamp or a timestamp before a shipper box was sealed are retained and visibly marked, but excluded from temperature calculations.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A reading from an unknown device or a source other than the supplier gateway is not accepted as a trusted reading.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A device with no reading for 15 minutes is shown as silent; if its logger is on a delivery route, an alert is raised.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-6\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Authorized users see a shared current record of stock quantities and statuses, orders and allocations, and temperature histories, rather than independently editable warehouse copies.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user can view temperature history for a box, cold room, or lot as a chart or table, with temperature bands, excursions, and missing-reading gaps identified.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock receipt, movement, allocation, temperature, and decision records remain associated with the relevant lot, handling unit, warehouse, order, or delivery so that the history can be traced.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Concurrent orders cannot cause the same physical stock quantity to be promised to more than one order.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-7\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Meridian staff can sign in only with a Meridian Microsoft account; staff-role sign-in from other organizations is refused.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer users sign in with their organisation account credentials and must complete a one-time-code second step before gaining access; a failed or missing second step leaves the account unauthenticated.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer account belongs to one customer organisation and cannot view another organisation's orders, deliveries, or documents; customer administrators can invite or remove users only in their own organisation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can view records only for warehouses to which they are assigned; quality managers and auditors can view records across all warehouses.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A staff member can hold more than one role, and available actions reflect the roles held and warehouse permissions.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An auditor can inspect records and audit history but any attempt to create, change, or delete a record is refused.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Removing or disabling a user revokes access immediately when their device is online, including a driver's signed-in web session.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Access attempts with invalid credentials or insufficient permissions do not expose protected records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-8\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An administrator can define a product's name, code, pack size, storage temperature band, and stability-budget tiers before saving; a product without a profile cannot be saved.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each profile tier defines an allowance in hours and minutes or is marked not permitted; the profile must cover the ranges adjoining the storage band without gaps or overlapping tiers.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A profile change requires a reason and effective date and creates a new version recording who made it; prior versions remain viewable and cannot be edited.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system assesses temperatures and accumulated time against the profile version effective for the applicable period; time in each tier consumes that tier's allowance, and a not-permitted range prevents release except through the specified two-person quality decision.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can list and search products by name or code; an administrator can deactivate a product, after which customers cannot order it.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An invalid or incomplete profile, overlapping tiers, or a gap between the band and not-permitted ranges is rejected with the problem identified.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-9\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A warehouse operator records a receipt's product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, cold room, and shelf; repeated receipts for the same product and lot number remain separately traceable while reports can show them together.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The operator can upload the manufacturer's inbound logger file; the resulting inbound budget usage is shown to quality staff before the release decision.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Every received quantity starts Quarantined and is unavailable for order allocation until a quality officer releases it.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A quality officer can release eligible quarantined stock after review; stock arriving within 30 days of expiry cannot be released.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A receipt with an expiry date in the past is refused; stock whose expiry date has passed becomes Expired automatically and is removed from allocations, with the dispatcher notified.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A stock movement between shelves or cold rooms records who moved it, when, and its origin and destination.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can see lot status among Quarantined, Released, On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, and Expired, and only Released stock is eligible for allocation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-10\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer user submits an order with at least one product line, at least one pack per line, a saved organisation delivery address, requested delivery date, and a choice of deliver-what-is-available or deliver-complete-only.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The earliest selectable delivery date follows the serving warehouse's configured cut-off, working days, and public holidays: before the cut-off permits the next working day, while after it permits no earlier than the following working day.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"After submission, the customer can see order status and each line's allocated and outstanding quantities as the order progresses through its applicable statuses.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The customer can change or cancel an order until packing begins; afterward the customer cannot do so, and only a dispatcher may cancel it.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Cancelling an order returns its allocated stock to available stock; the customer is not shown the order as cancelled if the cancellation failed.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A duplicate submission caused by a repeated tap creates only one order.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system refuses orders with no lines, a line quantity below one, a deactivated product, or a delivery date earlier than allowed, and explains the invalid input or date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-11\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On submission, the system allocates from released stock at the customer's serving warehouse, choosing suitable lots by earliest expiry first and splitting a line across lots when needed.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A lot is skipped when its expiry would leave less than the customer's required minimum shelf life on the requested delivery date; for equal expiry dates, the lot with more stability budget used is selected first.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system never allocates more than physically available stock or allocates a unit to two orders, including when orders are submitted concurrently.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A deliver-what-is-available order can be partly allocated, with the remainder waiting as a back order; a deliver-complete-only order holds no stock unless every line can be fully allocated.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When suitable stock is released, eligible back orders are filled automatically in submission order.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dispatcher may replace the selected lot for a line only with a recorded reason; an override that uses unreleased stock or breaches minimum shelf life is refused.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When allocated stock becomes On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, or Expired, it is removed from the order, replacement allocation is attempted, and the dispatcher is told the result.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can view available, allocated, quarantined, and on-hand quantities by product, lot, and warehouse; the displayed categories reconcile to quantity on hand.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-12\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A warehouse operator packs picked stock into a shipper box, recording its type, lot-level contents and quantities, and exactly one scanned logger when the box is sealed; sealing also records the time and operator.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A box can contain multiple products and lots for one delivery stop only when their storage bands match and the box type is qualified for that band.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A logger already assigned to another open box cannot be assigned again; a box cannot be sealed without exactly one logger.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dispatcher creates a dated route with one vehicle, one driver, at least one ordered stop, and a planned arrival time for each stop; the dispatcher determines stop order rather than the system optimizing it.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system refuses overlapping route assignments for the same driver or vehicle.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Before route confirmation, the system checks each box's planned arrival against its qualified duration minus the configured safety margin; if it fails, confirmation is refused and the affected box and amount of overrun are shown.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dispatcher can move a stop to another route or reorder it only until the driver has left for that stop; a confirmed-route change is communicated to the driver.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-13\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system accepts gateway batches of readings arriving late, duplicated, out of order, or in a large delayed batch, and produces the same time-ordered temperature history irrespective of arrival order.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A duplicate reading is stored once; a late or out-of-order valid reading is placed at its measurement time and affected temperature calculations and excursion records are brought up to date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A future-dated reading or a reading from before its box was sealed is retained with a visible invalid-for-calculation marker rather than silently discarded or used in calculations.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A 15-minute absence of readings is displayed as device silence; a gap is shown in history and is not assumed to have been within the permitted temperature band.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Authorized users can inspect temperature history for a box, cold room, or lot in chart and table views with the band and excursions marked.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-14\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An excursion opens on the first out-of-band reading and closes after three consecutive in-band readings; time is charged tier by tier to every affected handling unit that was in the box or cold room at that time.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system combines inbound, cold-room, and shipper-box exposure for each handling unit while retaining distinct histories and budgets for different parts of the same lot.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For an excursion on a route, the driver, dispatcher, and warehouse quality officers receive an alert within two minutes of the reading being received; alerts are also sent when a tier's remaining allowance falls below 25%, when a tier is exhausted, or when a not-permitted range is reached.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock affected by an open or undecided excursion is automatically placed On Hold and cannot be handed over pending a quality decision.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Late readings that lengthen, shorten, or remove an excursion update budgets, holds, and the excursion record, with the correction recorded in the audit trail.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a late reading reveals an excursion on already delivered stock, the system opens a quality review case and makes it visible to the customer.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-15\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A driver can open the assigned current-day route, see its stops and delivery work, and record loading, route progress, and delivery handover from a phone-sized responsive web experience.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The driver can continue working the route without network coverage and record handover details for later synchronization; the interface indicates which entries are pending synchronization.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system records delivery handover against the relevant stop and its boxes and stock so the delivery evidence can be traced to the customer and product history.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A driver cannot hand over stock on hold because of an open or undecided excursion, and the attempted handover is refused with the blocked stock identified.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If route access or an action cannot be confirmed while offline, the driver is shown the pending or unconfirmed state rather than a false server confirmation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The phone-based driver experience is part of the responsive web app and supports offline work; it is not a native iOS or Android application.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-16\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can use the staff and customer portals in English or Arabic, and portal text and controls display in the selected language where translations are provided.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When Arabic is selected, the interface is laid out right to left and remains usable at phone, tablet, and desktop widths.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Changing language does not change the user's organisation, role permissions, orders, stock, or other saved records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-17\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A quality manager can start a recall for a lot; the system shows the lot's remaining Meridian-held stock and the units delivered to each customer, and blocks remaining stock from allocation or handover.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system tracks each affected customer's response and the quantities accounted for until every recalled unit is accounted for.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can see which affected units remain held, were delivered, or still require customer response; a recall can be closed by a quality manager when the recall process is complete.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A recalled lot is excluded from new allocations, and any stock already allocated is removed from affected orders with replacement allocation attempted and the dispatcher notified.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff use one connected workflow to receive and track stock, process customer orders, allocate and pack stock, plan and record deliveries, monitor temperatures, make quality decisions, and manage recalls.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The record for a handling unit carries its traceable history from receipt through storage and delivery, including readings, budget use, holds, decisions, and handover.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When stock becomes unavailable or unsafe, the affected allocations and delivery work are updated and relevant staff are told; the system does not silently continue with an invalid allocation or release.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Warehouse operators can record receipts, stock movements, picks, and packing for warehouses they are assigned to.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Dispatchers can allocate or override stock with a reason, plan routes, assign drivers and vehicles, and monitor delivery progress for warehouses they can access.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Quality officers can review excursions and propose stock dispositions; Quality Managers can approve decisions and manage recalls; System Administrators can manage system configuration and accounts.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Auditors can view records and the audit trail across warehouses but cannot create, change, or delete records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The portal remains usable at phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user without the required role or warehouse assignment is denied the attempted action or access to that warehouse's data.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-3\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer users can create orders for their organisation, choose a saved delivery address and requested date, select complete-only or deliver-available treatment, and view order status and line allocations.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer users can change or cancel their orders until packing begins; after packing, a customer cancellation or change is refused.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer users can view deliveries, relevant delivery documents, and quality cases concerning their organisation, but cannot view another organisation's records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Customer Administrator can invite or remove users only within their own organisation; attempts to manage another organisation's users are denied.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer portal user cannot order a deactivated product, submit an empty order, or request a quantity below one pack.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-4\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A signed-in driver can open today's assigned route and access its stops and delivery details without a network connection during the working day.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"While offline, driver route actions and delivery records are retained for later synchronization; when connectivity returns, they are submitted and reflected in the shared delivery record.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If offline actions cannot be synchronized or conflict with a route change, the driver is shown that the action remains unconfirmed or needs attention rather than being told it succeeded on the shared record.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a driver's account is disabled or removed, access is revoked when the device is online; offline access does not make the account usable indefinitely beyond its working-day session.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treat the requested offline driver experience as the same responsive web app, with offline access to today's route and queued actions that synchronize when online, rather than a native mobile application.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-5\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system accepts temperature readings supplied through the logger gateway for known logger and cold-room sensor devices, and associates each reading with its device, measurement time, and temperature.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Readings from unknown devices or submissions not received through the authorized gateway are rejected and do not alter temperature history.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can view the temperature history for a box, cold room, or lot as a chart and table, with the applicable band and excursions shown.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a device has sent no reading for 15 minutes, it is shown as silent; a silent logger on an out-for-delivery box raises an alert.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-6\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A stock, order, delivery, and temperature change recorded by an authorized user is reflected in the shared record used by the relevant portals, rather than requiring users to reconcile separate copies.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system stores stock by product, lot, receipt, warehouse, and handling unit, and records orders, allocations, route and handover information, and temperature history against the relevant records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Changes to regulated records and quality decisions retain who made the change and when, and are available in the audit trail.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-7\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Meridian staff can sign in only with a Meridian Microsoft account; accounts from other organizations are not accepted for staff roles.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer users sign in with their organization's account credentials and must complete a one-time-code second step before access is granted; each customer user is associated with exactly one customer organization.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A staff member may hold multiple roles and sees stock, orders, and routes only for assigned warehouses; Quality Managers and Auditors can see all warehouses.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer users can access only their own organization's orders, deliveries, and documents. A cross-organization request is denied and does not disclose the other organization's data.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Auditor access is read-only, and attempts to create, edit, or delete records are denied.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A removed or disabled user loses access immediately when online, including on a signed-in driver web session.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invalid credentials or an incomplete or incorrect customer second-step code do not grant access.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-8\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A System Administrator can define a product's name, code, pack size, storage band, and stability-budget tiers, including an allowance or a not-permitted designation for each range.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system refuses to save a product without a temperature profile, with overlapping tiers, or with gaps between the band and the defined ranges.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A profile change requires a reason and effective date, creates a new version attributed to its author, and leaves earlier versions viewable but not editable.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A temperature in a not-permitted tier marks the affected product stock as not releasable except through the specified two-person quality decision.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can search and list products by name or code; an administrator can deactivate a product, after which customers cannot order it.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-9\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Warehouse Operator can record a receipt with product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, cold room, and shelf, and upload the manufacturer's inbound logger file.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each receipt is tracked separately even if the same product and lot number have been received before; reports can aggregate those receipts.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Newly received stock is Quarantined. A Quality Officer can review the inbound budget use and release eligible stock; only Released stock is available for allocation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A receipt with an expiry date in the past is refused, and stock arriving within 30 days of expiry cannot be released.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock movements between shelves or cold rooms record who moved it, when, and the origin and destination.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock automatically becomes Expired at the end of its expiry date, is removed from allocations, and the dispatcher is notified.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-10\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Customer User can submit an order with one or more product lines, each for at least one pack, a saved address belonging to the organization, and a requested delivery date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The selectable earliest delivery date follows the serving warehouse's configured cut-off, working days, and public holidays; before cut-off an eligible order can be for the next working day, and after cut-off no earlier than the following working day.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The customer chooses whether available quantities may be delivered partially or the order must be delivered complete.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The customer sees order status and allocated and outstanding quantity per line; the order progresses through applicable allocation, packing, delivery, and cancellation statuses.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer can change or cancel an order before packing begins. After packing, customer changes and cancellation are refused; a dispatcher may cancel it.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Cancelling an order returns its allocated stock to availability.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Submitting the same order twice through a duplicate submission, such as a double tap, creates only one order.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An order with no lines, a line below one pack, an unavailable delivery address, or an ineligible requested date is not accepted.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-11\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On submission, eligible Released stock is allocated from the customer's serving warehouse, earliest expiry first, excluding lots that fail the customer's minimum remaining shelf-life requirement on the requested delivery date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Where lots have the same expiry date, stock with more stability budget used is allocated first; a line may be split across lots, but no more than the physically available unallocated quantity is reserved.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An order marked deliver-available may be partly allocated and its remainder waits as a back order; when suitable stock is released, back orders are filled oldest submission first.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A complete-only order reserves no stock unless all its lines can be fully allocated.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dispatcher can override a lot choice only with a reason; the system refuses an override using non-Released stock or violating minimum shelf life.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When allocated stock is put On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, or Expired, it is removed from the order, replacement allocation is attempted, and the dispatcher is told the outcome.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can view available, allocated, and quarantined quantities by product, lot, and warehouse; these quantities reconcile to quantity on hand.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-12\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Warehouse Operator can pick allocated stock and pack a stop's stock into a shipper box; the box can contain multiple products and lots only when their storage bands match.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system refuses packing when a product's storage band differs from the other contents or is not supported by the box type's temperature range.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A box cannot be sealed without exactly one scanned logger, and the same logger cannot be assigned to two open boxes.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Sealing records its time, operator, logger, box type, and contents by lot and quantity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Dispatcher can create a dated route with at least one stop, one vehicle, one driver, and a planned arrival time for each stop; the dispatcher sets stop order.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system prevents a driver or vehicle from being assigned to overlapping routes and refuses confirmation when a box's planned arrival exceeds its qualified duration less the safety margin, identifying the box and excess time.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Dispatcher can move or reorder a stop until the driver has left for that stop; changes to a confirmed route are communicated to its driver.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-13\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system accepts known-device readings from the authorized supplier gateway, including batched readings, and stores each reading once when the same reading is received more than once.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A late or out-of-order reading is placed at its measurement time, and affected histories and calculations are recomputed so the resulting history does not depend on arrival order.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A reading timestamped in the future or before its box was sealed is retained with a marked status but excluded from calculations.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Periods without readings are displayed as gaps and are not treated as in-range time.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system handles readings from the stated population of 5,000 devices reporting at once without silently dropping accepted readings.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A duplicate reading does not create a second record or charge the stability budget twice.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-14\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a valid reading is outside a product's band, the system opens an excursion; it closes after three consecutive readings are back inside the band.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system charges excursion time to each affected handling unit, tier by tier, including inbound, cold-room, and box exposure; separate handling units from the same lot retain separate budget histories.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system shows used and remaining allowance by tier and the excursions responsible for the use; it alerts when a tier falls below 25% remaining, when a tier is exhausted, and when a not-permitted range is reached.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Within two minutes of receiving a reading that opens an excursion, the driver on the route, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers are alerted; affected stock is automatically placed On Hold until a quality decision is made.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Late readings that discover, lengthen, shorten, or remove an excursion update the excursion record, budget, holds, and alerts as appropriate, and the correction is recorded in the audit trail.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A late reading revealing an excursion on already-delivered stock opens a quality-review case and makes it visible to the customer concerned.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-15\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A driver can open the assigned route on a phone-sized web experience, view stops and box details, and record loading, journey progress, and delivery handover, including a recipient acknowledgment or signature where required.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Driver actions made without a connection are retained and later synchronized, so a handover recorded offline appears in the shared delivery record once synchronized.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A driver cannot hand over stock that is On Hold or otherwise not cleared for delivery; the attempted handover is refused and the driver is shown why.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A delivery record identifies the route, stop, delivered quantities, handover time, and recorded recipient acknowledgment; outstanding or undelivered quantities remain visible for follow-up.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If route details change after confirmation, the driver is notified when connected; an offline driver sees the change when the web experience next synchronizes.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treat the phone-based driver experience as the responsive web app with offline route access and queued actions. The available request text ends before the detailed US-009 acceptance criteria, so limit handover behaviours to those stated or directly implied by recording delivery handovers.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-16\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can use the warehouse and customer portals in English or Arabic.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When Arabic is selected, portal content is displayed right to left; when English is selected, it is displayed left to right.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Language selection does not change the user's organization, role, warehouse permissions, or underlying records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-17\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Quality Manager can start a recall for a lot and later close it; the system identifies every affected unit and where it is held or was delivered.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock Meridian still holds from a recalled lot is marked Recalled and blocked from allocation, packing, and handover.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For delivered units, the system identifies the receiving customer and tracks that customer's recall response against the quantity requiring accounting.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The recall remains open with outstanding customer responses or unaccounted units visible until every affected unit is accounted for; a Quality Manager can close it when complete.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff use one shared platform to receive and locate stock, process customer orders, allocate and pack stock, plan and follow deliveries, review temperature history and excursions, make quality decisions, and manage recalls.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The platform shows linked stock, order, delivery, temperature and quality records so users can trace a unit through those workflows.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Warehouse operators, dispatchers, quality staff, administrators and auditors can use the staff portal in a phone, tablet or desktop browser; controls remain touch-usable on narrow screens.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Warehouse operators can perform receiving, put-away, picking and packing; dispatchers can plan routes and monitor deliveries; quality staff can review excursions and decisions; administrators can manage authorized configuration; auditors can inspect records without changing them.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff see records only for warehouses they are assigned to, except Quality Managers and Auditors, who can see all warehouses.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-3\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer users can use a responsive browser portal to place orders and view their own orders, line allocations, outstanding quantities, deliveries and relevant documents.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer user sees only records belonging to their own customer organisation; attempts to access another organisation's records do not disclose them.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Customer Administrator can invite or remove users only for their own organisation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-4\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A signed-in driver can open and work the current day's route in a phone browser when offline, including viewing its stops and recording route and handover actions.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Driver actions entered without a connection are retained and synchronized when connectivity returns; the resulting shared route and delivery records reflect the queued actions.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When the device is online, a removed or disabled user's access is revoked, including driver access.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Driver mobile application means the same responsive, installable web app in a phone browser, not a native app.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-5\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The platform accepts temperature readings from the logger supplier's gateway for known data loggers and cold-room sensors, and associates each reading with its device, recorded time and temperature.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Readings from an unknown device or received through a channel other than the supplier gateway are rejected.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can view sensor and logger histories for the relevant cold room, box or stock, including gaps and marked excursions.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-6\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Changes to stock, orders and temperature history are reflected in one shared record so authorized users see current quantities, statuses and histories rather than separate spreadsheet copies.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can trace stock by product, lot, receipt and handling unit and view its temperature history across receipt, storage and delivery.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The platform records who performed regulated actions and when, and exposes that history for inspection.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-7\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Meridian staff authenticate with a Meridian Microsoft account; a non-Meridian account cannot sign in as staff. Customer users authenticate with email and password and must complete a one-time-code second step.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A staff member may hold multiple roles and sees only assigned warehouses; Quality Managers and Auditors can see all warehouses. A customer account belongs to exactly one organisation and sees only that organisation's records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer Administrators can invite and remove users only within their own organisation. Removed or disabled users lose access immediately when online, including on a signed-in driver device.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Auditors can view records and the audit trail but cannot create, change or delete records; attempts to do so are refused.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A signed-in driver can access today's route for the working day without a connection.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-8\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An administrator can create a product only with a temperature profile defining its storage band and stability-budget tiers, including an allowance or a not-permitted designation for each range.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system refuses a profile with overlapping tiers or gaps between the band and the not-permitted ranges, and refuses to save a product without a profile.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A profile change requires a reason and effective date, creates a new version attributed to its author, and leaves earlier versions viewable but uneditable.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can list and search products by name or code. An administrator can deactivate a product; a deactivated product cannot be ordered.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A reading in a not-permitted range prevents ordinary release; release requires the full two-person decision described for quality decisions.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-9\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A warehouse operator records each receipt's product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, cold room and shelf; repeated receipts of the same product and lot number remain separately traceable while being reportable together.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The operator can upload the manufacturer's inbound logger file, and the system calculates and displays inbound stability-budget use for the quality review.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A new receipt starts Quarantined. A Quality Officer can review it and release eligible stock; only Released stock becomes available for allocation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system refuses receipt of stock whose expiry date is in the past and refuses release when the stock was within 30 days of expiry on arrival.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system changes stock to Expired at the end of its expiry date, removes it from allocations, and informs the dispatcher.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When an operator moves stock between shelves or cold rooms, the system records the actor, time, source and destination.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-10\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer user can submit an order with one or more product lines, at least one pack per line, a saved address belonging to the organisation, a requested delivery date and a choice of deliver-available or deliver-complete-only.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The selectable earliest delivery date follows the serving warehouse's configured cut-off, working days and public holidays; orders before the cut-off can be due next working day, while later orders are due no earlier than the following working day.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system refuses an empty order, a line quantity below one pack, an address not saved for the organisation, or an order for a deactivated product.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A double submission of the same order, such as a double tap, creates one order rather than duplicate orders.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customers can view order status and each line's allocated and outstanding quantities. They can change or cancel an order until packing begins; after packing begins, customer changes and cancellation are refused.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dispatcher, but not the customer, can cancel an order after packing begins. Cancelling returns allocated stock to availability.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-11\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On submission, the system allocates only Released stock from the customer's serving warehouse, selecting eligible lots by earliest expiry; equal-expiry lots are ordered with the lot having more stability budget used first.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system skips a lot that would fail the customer's minimum remaining shelf-life requirement on the requested delivery date, never allocates more than physically available, and displays any line split across multiple lots.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system prevents simultaneous orders from allocating the same stock unit twice.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A deliver-available order can be Partly Allocated, with its unfilled quantity waiting as a back order; when eligible stock is released, back orders are filled automatically in submission order.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A deliver-complete-only order holds no stock unless every line can be fully allocated.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dispatcher can override a lot choice only with a reason; the system refuses an override that selects non-Released stock or violates minimum shelf life.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If allocated stock becomes On Hold, Rejected, Recalled or Expired, the system removes it from the order, attempts replacement allocation and informs the dispatcher of the outcome.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can view available, allocated and quarantined quantities by product, lot and warehouse; those categories reconcile to quantity on hand.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-12\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A warehouse operator can pack a stop's stock into a shipper box and scan exactly one logger before sealing; sealing records the time, operator, logger and contents by lot and quantity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system refuses sealing without exactly one logger and prevents a logger from being assigned to two open boxes at once.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system refuses to pack products with different storage bands in one box or a product whose band is not supported by that box type.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dispatcher can create a dated route with one vehicle, one driver and at least one ordered stop, and enter each stop's planned arrival time.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system refuses overlapping route assignments for a driver or vehicle. It also refuses route confirmation when a box's planned arrival exceeds its qualified duration minus the configured safety margin, identifying the box and excess time.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dispatcher can reorder a stop or move it to another route until the driver has left for that stop; a confirmed-route change is communicated to the driver.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-13\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system accepts readings in batches, stores a repeated reading only once, and places late or out-of-order readings at their recorded event time so history and dependent calculations are recomputed consistently.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A future-dated reading or a reading taken before its box was sealed is retained and marked, but excluded from temperature calculations.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"After 15 minutes without a reading, the device is shown as silent; silence from a logger in a box out for delivery raises an alert.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No-reading intervals appear as gaps and are not treated as in-range time. Users can view a box, cold-room or lot history as a chart and table with the band and excursions marked.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The service can accept the specified reporting load of 5,000 devices reporting at once.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-14\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a reading is outside a stored product's temperature band, the system opens an excursion; it closes only after three consecutive readings are back inside the band.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system charges excursion time tier by tier against each affected handling unit's stability budget, combining recorded inbound, cold-room and shipper-box exposure while keeping distinct handling units' histories separate.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system displays used and remaining allowance for every tier and the excursions that consumed it; it alerts when an allowance falls below 25%, when a tier is exhausted, and when a not-permitted range is reached.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Within two minutes of receiving the reading that opens an excursion, the system alerts the driver for an on-route box, the dispatcher and the warehouse's Quality Officers.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock affected by an open or undecided excursion is automatically placed On Hold and cannot be handed over until a quality decision is made.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When late readings alter, lengthen, shorten or remove an excursion, the system recalculates budgets and holds, updates the excursion record and records the correction in the audit trail.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A late reading that reveals an excursion in already-delivered stock opens a quality-review case and makes the case visible to the customer.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-15\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A driver can use a phone browser to view the assigned route, load shipper boxes, drive the route and record delivery handovers; the handover record provides evidence of delivery, including the customer's sign-off.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The driver can perform route and handover work without network coverage; offline actions are retained and synchronized when a connection returns.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The driver is notified of changes to a confirmed route and receives relevant on-route temperature alerts.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system prevents a driver from acting on routes they are not assigned to, and a disabled or removed account cannot continue to access the service when online.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The named driver mobile application is delivered as the responsive web app in a phone browser; offline support applies to today's route and recorded driver actions.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-16\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can use the staff and customer portals in English or Arabic.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When Arabic is selected, portal content is displayed right to left and controls and navigation follow the right-to-left layout.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-17\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Quality Manager can start and close a recall for a lot; the system identifies where every unit is or went, including stock still held and units delivered to customers.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system blocks Meridian-held stock in a recalled lot from allocation or delivery and shows its recalled status.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The platform tracks each affected customer's response and the units accounted for, showing what remains outstanding until every unit is accounted for.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Recall actions and associated records remain available for authorized review and audit.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"differences\" kind=\"differences\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"D-2\",\n  \"span\": \"I-4\",\n  \"topic\": \"Offline driver actions after account disablement\",\n  \"readings\": [\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 1,\n    \"behaviour\": 2,\n    \"summary\": \"Offline queued actions are not treated as authorized once the system can verify a disabled or removed account.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 2,\n    \"behaviour\": 3,\n    \"summary\": \"Offline access does not make a disabled account usable indefinitely beyond its working-day session.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 3,\n    \"behaviour\": 1,\n    \"summary\": \"Offline actions are retained and synchronized when connectivity returns, without specifying rejection based on later account disablement.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"D-3\",\n  \"span\": \"I-9\",\n  \"topic\": \"Inbound logger budget review before release\",\n  \"readings\": [\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 1,\n    \"behaviour\": 1,\n    \"summary\": \"Inbound logger file upload makes resulting inbound budget usage visible to quality staff before release decision.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 2,\n    \"behaviour\": 0,\n    \"summary\": \"Receipt can include an inbound logger file, while review of inbound budget use is not specified as a required pre-release step.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 3,\n    \"behaviour\": 1,\n    \"summary\": \"Uploaded inbound logger file is used to calculate and display budget use for quality review.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"D-4\",\n  \"span\": \"I-11\",\n  \"topic\": \"Quantity reconciliation includes physically on-hand category\",\n  \"readings\": [\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 1,\n    \"behaviour\": 7,\n    \"summary\": \"Users view available, allocated, quarantined, and on-hand quantities, reconciling categories to on-hand.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 2,\n    \"behaviour\": 6,\n    \"summary\": \"Users view available, allocated, and quarantined quantities, reconciling them to quantity on hand; no separate on-hand category is specified.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 3,\n    \"behaviour\": 7,\n    \"summary\": \"Users view available, allocated, and quarantined quantities, reconciling those categories to quantity on hand.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"D-5\",\n  \"span\": \"I-12\",\n  \"topic\": \"Box packing limited to a single delivery stop\",\n  \"readings\": [\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 1,\n    \"behaviour\": 1,\n    \"summary\": \"A box may contain multiple products and lots for one delivery stop only when storage bands match and box type is qualified.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 2,\n    \"behaviour\": 0,\n    \"summary\": \"A box packs a stop's stock and applies storage-band and box-type compatibility, without explicitly stating a one-stop-only constraint.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 3,\n    \"behaviour\": 0,\n    \"summary\": \"A box packs a stop's stock with logger and traceability requirements; no explicit cross-stop restriction is stated.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"D-6\",\n  \"span\": \"I-14\",\n  \"topic\": \"Timing of quality holds versus excursion alerts\",\n  \"readings\": [\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 1,\n    \"behaviour\": 2,\n    \"summary\": \"Route excursion alerts are sent within two minutes of the reading being received.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 2,\n    \"behaviour\": 3,\n    \"summary\": \"Within two minutes of receiving an excursion-opening reading, relevant staff are alerted and affected stock is put On Hold.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 3,\n    \"behaviour\": 3,\n    \"summary\": \"Alerts are sent within two minutes, while hold behavior is stated separately for affected stock.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"D-7\",\n  \"span\": \"I-15\",\n  \"topic\": \"Evidence required for delivery handover\",\n  \"readings\": [\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 1,\n    \"behaviour\": 2,\n    \"summary\": \"Handover is recorded against stop, boxes, and stock for traceability, without requiring recipient acknowledgment or signature.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 2,\n    \"behaviour\": 0,\n    \"summary\": \"Handover includes recipient acknowledgment or signature where required, and behavior 3 records that acknowledgment.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 3,\n    \"behaviour\": 0,\n    \"summary\": \"Handover evidence includes the customer's sign-off.\"\n   }\n  ]\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<untrusted_document id=\"request\" source=\"cli\">\nMeridian ColdChain Platform\n\nIntroduction\n\nMeridian Healthcare Distribution supplies vaccines, insulin, biologics and other temperature-sensitive\nmedicines to around 400 hospitals, pharmacies and clinics. Stock is held in three warehouses (Karachi,\nLahore and Dubai) and delivered by Meridian's own vans in insulated shipper boxes.\n\nEvery one of these products has a storage temperature band, for example 2 °C to 8 °C. A product that\nspends too long outside its band may lose potency without any visible sign. Regulators require Meridian\nto prove, for every unit it hands over, that the product stayed within its permitted conditions from the\nmoment Meridian received it until the customer signed for it.\n\nToday this proof is assembled by hand. Cold rooms are checked on paper twice a day. Each shipper box\ncarries a data logger that is plugged into a computer after the van returns. Stock is tracked in\nspreadsheets per warehouse. Delivery notes are signed on paper.\n\nMeridian plans to replace this with a single platform covering stock, orders, deliveries, live temperature\nmonitoring, quality decisions and recalls.\n\nProblem Statement\n\nThe current process does not tell anyone that a product is at risk until it is too late to act.\n\nAs a result:\n\n● A temperature problem in a van is discovered hours after the product has been handed to the\ncustomer.\n● Quality staff cannot tell how much time outside its band a product has already used up, so they\neither write off good stock or release stock on judgement alone.\n● Stock nearest its expiry date is not reliably sent out first, and customers receive product with too\nlittle shelf life left.\n● Two people working from different copies of a spreadsheet promise the same stock to two\ncustomers.\n● When a manufacturer recalls a lot, finding every customer who received it takes two to three days.\n● Records can be changed after the fact, and an inspector cannot be shown who decided what and\nwhen.\n● Drivers lose mobile signal in basements, hospital loading bays and on long routes, so anything that\ndepends on a live connection fails exactly where it is needed.\n\nSolution Overview\n\nThe proposed solution will consist of:\n\n● A web portal for warehouse staff, dispatchers, quality staff, administrators and auditors.\n● A customer portal for hospitals, pharmacies and clinics.\n● A driver mobile application for iOS and Android that keeps working without a connection.\n● A service that receives temperature readings from data loggers and cold-room sensors.\n● A centralized backend system holding one shared record of stock, orders and temperature history.\n\nMeridian staff will sign in with their Meridian Microsoft account. Customer users are invited by their\nown organisation and see only their own organisation's orders and deliveries.\n\nEach product has a temperature profile: its storage band and a stability budget, which is the total time\nthe product is allowed to spend outside the band over its whole life, split by how far outside it went.\nThe system keeps a running account of the budget each handling unit has used, from receipt to delivery.\n\nStock is received in lots. Customers order by product and quantity. The system decides which lots to\nsend, earliest expiry first. Picked stock is packed into shipper boxes, each with a data logger, and the\nboxes are loaded onto a route.\n\nLoggers report a reading every 5 minutes. When a reading falls outside the band, the system opens an\nexcursion, charges the time against the budget of everything in that box, and alerts the driver, the\ndispatcher and quality staff. Affected stock cannot be handed over until quality staff have decided\nwhat happens to it.\n\nWhen a lot is recalled, the system shows where every unit of it is or went, blocks what Meridian still\nholds, and tracks each customer's response until every unit is accounted for.\n\nThe portals shall be available in English and Arabic. Arabic is shown right to left.\n\nUser Roles\n\nWarehouse Operator\n\nReceives stock, puts it away, picks and packs orders into shipper boxes.\n\nDispatcher\n\nPlans routes, assigns drivers and vehicles, and follows deliveries during the day.\n\nDriver\n\nLoads shipper boxes, drives the route and hands over deliveries using the mobile application.\n\nQuality Officer\n\nReviews excursions and proposes what happens to affected stock.\n\nQuality Manager\n\nApproves quality decisions and starts and closes recalls. Legally responsible for released stock.\n\nCustomer User\n\nA member of staff at a hospital, pharmacy or clinic who places orders and follows deliveries.\n\nCustomer Administrator\n\nA customer user who can also invite and remove users for their own organisation.\n\nSystem Administrator\n\nManages staff accounts, warehouses, vehicles, shipper box types, products and system configuration.\n\nAuditor\n\nAn internal or external inspector with read-only access to all records and the audit trail.\n\nUser Stories\n\nUS-001: Sign In and Access Control\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a user, I want to sign in securely and see only what my role and organisation allow so that\nregulated records are protected.\n\nDescription\n\nMeridian staff shall sign in with their Meridian Microsoft account. Accounts from other organisations\nshall not be accepted for staff roles.\n\nCustomer users shall sign in with an email address and password and a second step using a one-time\ncode. A customer user belongs to exactly one customer organisation.\n\nDrivers use the same Meridian account on the mobile application. Once signed in, the application shall\nremain usable for the working day without a connection.\n\nA staff member may hold more than one role. Each staff member belongs to one or more warehouses\nand sees only stock, orders and routes of those warehouses. Quality Managers and Auditors see all\nwarehouses.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● Staff can sign in only with a Meridian Microsoft account.\n● Customer users can sign in only after completing the second step.\n● A customer user never sees another organisation's orders, deliveries or documents.\n● A staff member sees only the warehouses they are assigned to.\n● A Customer Administrator can invite and remove users of their own organisation only.\n● A removed or disabled user loses access immediately, including on a mobile device that is online.\n● A signed-in driver can open and work today's route without a connection.\n● An Auditor cannot create, change or delete any record.\n\nUS-002: Products and Temperature Profiles\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a System Administrator, I want to define each product's temperature profile so that the system\ncan judge every reading against the right limits.\n\nDescription\n\nA product has a name, a code, a pack size and a temperature profile.\n\nA temperature profile consists of a storage band and a stability budget. The budget is expressed as\ntiers. For example, for a 2 °C to 8 °C product:\n\n● Above 8 °C up to 15 °C: 12 hours in total.\n● Above 15 °C up to 25 °C: 2 hours in total.\n● Above 25 °C: not permitted.\n● Below 2 °C down to 0 °C: 4 hours in total.\n● Below 0 °C: not permitted.\n\nTime spent in a tier counts against that tier's allowance. A reading in a not-permitted range means the\nproduct cannot be released by anyone other than through the full two-person decision in US-010.\n\nProfiles are versioned. Changing a profile requires a reason and takes effect from a stated date. Earlier\nversions remain viewable.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● A product cannot be saved without a temperature profile.\n● Tiers must not overlap and must leave no gap between the band and the not-permitted ranges.\n● Each tier has an allowance in hours and minutes, or is marked not permitted.\n● A profile change creates a new version with a reason, an effective date and the person who made\nit.\n● Earlier versions of a profile can be viewed but not changed.\n● Products can be listed, searched by name or code, and deactivated. A deactivated product cannot\nbe ordered.\n\nUS-003: Receive Stock\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a Warehouse Operator, I want to receive incoming stock by lot so that every unit is traceable\nfrom the moment it arrives.\n\nDescription\n\nStock arrives from manufacturers in lots. For each receipt the operator records the product, lot number,\nexpiry date, quantity, supplier and the cold room and shelf where it is stored.\n\nThe manufacturer's shipment arrives with its own logger. The operator uploads the logger's file, and\nthe system charges any time outside the band during the inbound journey against the lot's budget.\n\nAll received stock starts as Quarantined. A Quality Officer reviews the receipt and releases it, after\nwhich it is available to be allocated to orders. Stock within 30 days of expiry on arrival cannot be\nreleased.\n\nA lot can be in these statuses: Quarantined, Released, On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, Expired. Stock\nbecomes Expired automatically at the end of its expiry date.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● A receipt records product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier and storage location.\n● The same lot number for the same product can be received more than once, and the receipts are\ntracked separately but reported together.\n● Received stock is Quarantined until released by a Quality Officer.\n● The inbound logger file can be uploaded, and the budget used on the inbound journey is shown\nbefore the release decision.\n● Stock with an expiry date in the past cannot be received.\n● Stock within 30 days of expiry on arrival cannot be released.\n● Only Released stock can be allocated to an order.\n● Stock becomes Expired automatically and is removed from any allocation it was part of, and the\ndispatcher is told.\n● Moving stock between shelves or cold rooms is recorded with who, when, from and to.\n\nUS-004: Place an Order\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a Customer User, I want to order products for a delivery date so that my site receives what it\nneeds on time.\n\nDescription\n\nA customer user places an order made of one or more lines. Each line is a product and a quantity in\npacks. The order has a delivery address, chosen from the organisation's saved addresses, and a\nrequested delivery date.\n\nOrders placed before the cut-off time (default 14:00, configurable per warehouse) can be delivered the\nnext working day. Orders placed after the cut-off are delivered no earlier than the working day after\nthat. Working days and public holidays are configured per warehouse.\n\nEach customer organisation is served by one warehouse and has a minimum remaining shelf life (for\nexample 90 days) that any delivered product must have on the delivery date. The customer chooses\nper order whether a short order may be delivered in part or must be delivered complete.\n\nAn order moves through: Submitted, Allocated, Partly Allocated, Packed, Out for Delivery, Delivered,\nPartly Delivered, Cancelled. A customer can cancel or change an order until packing begins.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● An order has at least one line, and each line has a quantity of at least 1 pack.\n● The earliest selectable delivery date follows the cut-off time, working days and holidays of the\nserving warehouse.\n● The customer chooses between \"deliver what is available\" and \"deliver complete only\".\n● The customer sees the order status and each line's allocated and outstanding quantity.\n● An order can be changed or cancelled by the customer until it is Packed. After that, only a\ndispatcher can cancel it.\n● Cancelling an order returns its allocated stock to available stock.\n● Submitting the same order twice by mistake, for example by a double tap, creates one order.\n\nUS-005: Allocate Stock to Orders\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a Dispatcher, I want the system to choose which lots fulfil each order so that the oldest suitable\nstock goes out first and nothing is promised twice.\n\nDescription\n\nWhen an order is submitted, the system allocates stock to each line from the serving warehouse.\n\nAllocation rules:\n\n● Only Released stock is used.\n● The lot with the earliest expiry date is used first.\n● A lot is skipped for a customer if, on the requested delivery date, it would have less than that\ncustomer's minimum remaining shelf life.\n● Between two lots with the same expiry date, the one with more of its stability budget used is sent\nfirst.\n● A line may be fulfilled from more than one lot.\n● Stock is never allocated beyond what is physically available.\n\nIf a line cannot be fully allocated, an order marked \"deliver what is available\" is Partly Allocated and the\nremainder waits as a back order, which is filled automatically, oldest order first, when suitable stock is\nreleased. An order marked \"deliver complete only\" holds no stock until every line can be fully allocated.\n\nA dispatcher may override the system's choice of lot for a line, with a reason. An override may not\nbreak the Released-only rule or the customer's minimum shelf life.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● Allocation follows earliest-expiry-first within the rules above.\n● No unit of stock is ever allocated to two orders, including when many orders are submitted at the\nsame moment.\n● A line can be split across lots, and the split is visible on the order.\n● A \"deliver complete only\" order holds no stock until it can be fully allocated.\n● Back orders are filled automatically in the order they were submitted when stock becomes available.\n● A dispatcher override requires a reason and is refused if it breaks the Released-only rule or the\nminimum shelf life.\n● When allocated stock is put On Hold, Rejected, Recalled or Expired, it is removed from the order,\nthe system tries to allocate replacement stock, and the dispatcher is told the outcome.\n● Available, allocated and quarantined quantities per product, lot and warehouse can be viewed at\nany time and always add up to the quantity on hand.\n\nUS-006: Pack Shipper Boxes and Plan Routes\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a Dispatcher, I want to pack orders into shipper boxes and place them on routes so that every\nbox can keep its contents in range for the whole journey.\n\nDescription\n\nA Warehouse Operator picks the allocated lots and packs them into shipper boxes. Each box has a\ntype, and each type has a temperature range it is built for and a qualified duration (for example 48\nhours) for which it holds that range once sealed. Each packed box is given one data logger by scanning\nthe logger's barcode. A box holds stock for one delivery stop only, but may hold several products and\nlots, provided all of them share the same storage band.\n\nA dispatcher creates a route for a date with a vehicle, a driver and an ordered list of stops. Each stop\nhas a planned arrival time entered by the dispatcher. The system does not work out the best order of\nstops.\n\nA route cannot be confirmed if any box on it would reach its stop later than its qualified duration, less\na safety margin (default 4 hours, configurable), counted from the moment the box was sealed.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● A box cannot be sealed without exactly one logger, and a logger cannot be in two open boxes at\nonce.\n● A box cannot be packed with products whose storage bands differ, or with a product whose band\nthe box type is not built for.\n● Sealing a box records the time, the operator, the contents by lot and quantity, and the logger.\n● A route has one vehicle, one driver, a date and at least one stop.\n● A driver or vehicle cannot be on two routes whose times overlap.\n● A route is refused confirmation if a box would exceed its qualified duration less the safety margin\nat its planned arrival, and the screen says which box and by how much.\n● A dispatcher can move a stop to another route or reorder stops until the driver has left for that\nstop.\n● The driver is told of any change to a route that has already been confirmed.\n\nUS-007: Receive Temperature Readings\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a Quality Officer, I want every reading from every logger and cold-room sensor stored reliably\nso that the temperature history of any unit is complete and trustworthy.\n\nDescription\n\nLoggers in shipper boxes and fixed sensors in cold rooms take a reading every 5 minutes. Readings\nreach the system through the logger supplier's gateway, which sends them in batches. Each reading\ncarries the device identifier, the time the reading was taken and the temperature.\n\nThe mobile network is not reliable. Readings may arrive minutes or hours late, in the wrong order, more\nthan once, or in one large batch when a van comes back into coverage. The system shall produce the\nsame temperature history regardless of the order in which readings arrive.\n\nA device that has sent nothing for 15 minutes is treated as silent. A silent logger in a box that is out for\ndelivery raises an alert. Time with no readings is shown as a gap in the history and is not assumed to\nbe in range.\n\nThe system shall be sized for 5,000 devices reporting at once.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● Readings are accepted only from the supplier's gateway and only for known devices.\n● A reading received twice is stored once.\n● Readings that arrive late or out of order are placed at the time they were taken, and everything\ncalculated from them is brought up to date.\n● A reading with a time in the future, or from before the box was sealed, is kept but marked and not\nused in calculations.\n● A device with no reading for 15 minutes is shown as silent, and an alert is raised if its box is out for\ndelivery.\n● Gaps are visible in the temperature history as gaps.\n● The temperature history of any box, cold room or lot can be viewed as a chart and as a table, with\nthe band and the excursions marked.\n\nUS-008: Detect Excursions and Track the Stability Budget\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a Quality Officer, I want the system to detect excursions and keep each unit's remaining budget\nup to date so that I know immediately which stock is at risk and by how much.\n\nDescription\n\nAn excursion opens when a reading from a box or cold room is outside the band of a product stored\nin it. It closes when three readings in a row are back inside the band. The duration of the excursion is\ncharged, tier by tier, against the stability budget of every handling unit that was in that box or cold\nroom at the time.\n\nThe budget is tracked per handling unit, not per lot: two parts of the same lot that travelled in different\nboxes have different histories. The budget used in the manufacturer's inbound journey, in the cold\nroom and in every box is added together.\n\nWhen an excursion opens, the driver (if the box is on a route), the dispatcher and the Quality Officers\nof the warehouse are alerted within 2 minutes of the reading being received. A further alert is sent\nwhen the remaining allowance in any tier falls below 25%, and again when a tier is used up or a\nnot-permitted range is reached.\n\nAll stock affected by an open or undecided excursion is placed On Hold automatically.\n\nBecause readings can arrive late, an excursion may be discovered, lengthened, shortened or removed\nafter the event. Budgets, holds and alerts shall follow the corrected history.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● An excursion opens on the first reading outside the band and closes after three consecutive\nreadings inside it.\n● Excursion time is charged to the correct tier, and a single excursion that passes through several\ntiers is charged to each for the time spent in it.\n● The budget used and remaining per tier is shown for every handling unit, with the excursions that\nconsumed it.\n● Parts of one lot with different histories show different budgets.\n● Alerts reach the driver, dispatcher and Quality Officers within 2 minutes of the reading being\nreceived.\n● Stock affected by an excursion is On Hold until a decision is made under US-010.\n● Late readings that change an excursion update the budget, the holds and the excursion record,\nand the change is recorded in the audit trail.\n● A late reading that reveals an excursion on stock already delivered opens a case for quality review\nand is shown to the customer.\n\nUS-009: Deliver with the Driver Application\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a Driver, I want to load, drive and hand over my deliveries from my phone, with or without\nsignal, so that every handover is recorded properly.\n\nDescription\n</untrusted_document>\n\nList the questions."}